# Line endings.
#
# WordPress.org publishes themes over SVN, and a package that mixes DOS and UNIX
# line endings can fail to upload with no useful error. Every text file in this
# theme is therefore normalised to LF, in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# This lives here rather than in core.autocrlf on purpose: core.autocrlf is
# per-machine config that no clone inherits, so it makes the shipped zip depend on
# whose machine built it. `eol=lf` overrides core.autocrlf, so the result is the
# same on Windows, macOS, Linux and CI.
#
# release.sh rsyncs the WORKING TREE into the zip, so the working tree is what
# actually ships - which is why eol=lf matters here and not just text=auto.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touch these bytes.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.eot binary
*.mo binary

# Executable shell script: a stray CR after the shebang makes the kernel look for
# an interpreter whose name ends in \r ("bad interpreter"). Pinned explicitly.
*.sh text eol=lf
